		(uuid "532ed4ed-8d03-57be-ba58-1b7ca7a5ffca")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: LT3582-12 makes STIM_POS_12V (+12 V, boost through D11 to CAPP and its output-disconnect switch to VOUTP) and STIM_NEG_12V (-12 V, single-inductor inverter through D12) from VIN_3V3, as pre-regulators for the stimulation LDOs. Fixed +/-12 V with internal feedback and compensation; starts with EN_ASIC_RAILS (SHDN on above 1.1 V). About 10 mA per output.\n\n2. Source / changes: ADI LT3582/LT3582-5/LT3582-12 data sheet 3582512fb, Figure 13 p.22 (+/-12 V from a single 5 V input), Pin Functions p.8, Choosing Inductors p.18, Capacitor and Diode Selection p.19, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/3582512fb.pdf . Changed from Figure 13: input 3.3 V instead of 4.5-5.5 V (allowed 2.55-5.5 V; max load at 3.3 V about 40 mA per output from the p.19 equations, need about 10 mA); C1 -> C11 4.7 uF 10 V 0603; C2 -> C21 22 uF 25 V 0805 and C3 -> C14 22 uF 25 V 0805 (about 6-7 uF effective at 12 V, inside the 2.2-10 uF range); C4 -> C15 1 uF 25 V on CAPP; C5/C6 -> C16/C17 10 nF; L1/L2 6.8 uH (Coilcraft XPL2010-682 in the figure) -> L11/L12 TDK VLS201612HBX-6R8M-1, JLC C501945 (V35; before: Murata DFE201610E-6R8M=P2, which JLC does not list): 6.8 uH +/-20 %, Isat 0.91 A, Itemp 0.87 A, 0.468 ohm max, 1.2 mm high (TDK VLS201612HBX-1 data sheet, 20180709, p.1 table and p.3 drawings, https://datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/dce85b51190e1e89e74a90d08568b6cf.pdf ). Needed (p.3 current limits, p.18 equation IPK = ILIMIT + VIN x TOS / L): 0.48 A peak in L11 and 0.78 A in L12, 0.80 A with L 20 % low and 3.6 V in. TDK land pattern 0.5 x 1.6 mm pads, 2.0 mm over all; board pads 0.55 x 1.6 mm, 2.0 mm over all; D1/D2 Diodes Inc. B0540WS-7 in the figure -> D11/D12 MCC B0540WS-TP, JLC C668860 (V35; the Diodes part, JLC C98664, cannot be ordered at JLC): same type and case, 40 V, 0.5 A average, 5 A surge, 0.55 V max at 0.5 A, SOD-323 (MCC B0540WS data sheet Rev.3-2-07102019, p.1, https://datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/231bf9d51761a20ad69da348e7944c17.pdf ). Needed: 12.1 V reverse on D11 and 15.4 V on D12, average = the load of about 10 mA, peak as the inductors. Different from the Diodes part: leakage limit 80 uA at 40 V against 5 uA at 30 V (0.8 % of a 10 mA load); neither sheet gives a repetitive-peak rating. MCC leads 2.30-2.70 mm over all and 0.25-0.40 mm wide; board pads 0.60 x 0.45 mm, 2.70 mm over all; SHDN to EN_ASIC_RAILS instead of an input logic signal; CA/SDA/SCL to GND, VPP open (I2C/OTP unused on the -12 version). V24 replaces the TPS65130 (Howard, 8 Nov 2026: smaller parts) and removes R11-R15, C12, C13, C18-C20, C22. V34: the +/-12 V setting is unchanged; the LDOs after it are now set to +/-8.06 V. V35 (13 Nov 2026): part fields only, no net and no copper changed. U1 LT3582EUD-12#PBF is JLC C670975: 0 in JLC stock, so it comes through JLC Global Sourcing; only the -12 version works here. JLC stock read 13 Nov 2026, 00:12 CST: C668860 6,169 orderable, C501945 170 orderable (10 of each needed for 5 boards), C670975 0. Unverified: ripple after layout, start-up current at the J2 supply contacts, diode leakage when warm; nothing is measured yet. Option B LDO V3 (25 Nov 2026): unchanged from V24; U1 C670975 has 0 orderable at JLC (read 2026-11-25 07:31 CST), Global Sourcing / consignment required."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
