	(text "TP10: bottom-side pad, silk 5V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 449 541 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ec232fed-81d6-5201-a1d1-c6dcf8c5eb7a")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: Brings the Frontend's 5 V input (VIN_5V) onto this board on one contact, J1.32, and ends it on the test pad TP10. Nothing on this board uses it: it is a provision, so the regulation can be changed later without a new connector map.\n\n2. Source / changes: Claude design, no manufacturer reference circuit. Howard, 12 Nov 2026 (decision 4 after the meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), where the designer suggested also sending 5 V to the LDO board). Contact from pin map V6 (12 Nov 2026; 2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/09_Pin_Map_V6/PIN_MAP_V6.csv and ASIC_PORT_PINS_V6.csv; frozen 13 Nov 2026): J1.32 = VIN_5V with J1.30 (new GND) and J1.34 (GND) as row neighbours, so a solder bridge cannot put 5 V on a 1.5 V line. One DF40 contact is rated 0.3 A (Hirose DF40 catalog, https://datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/145ab5d527b34eafa7a47375cb561c6a.pdf?productCode=C3640153 ). No capacitor: the net has no load here. Layout V13: 0.20 mm on L1 between the two J1 contact rows, 0.29 mm from the inner ends of the 1.5 V contacts 34-68. Unverified: the Frontend does not drive J1.32 yet (its next revision does); the load of any later 5 V use."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 480 524 0)
		(size 150 40.5)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
